SpecQR Julia
Copyright (c) 2026 SpecQR contributors

Full-scratch Julia implementation of the user-owned SpecQR QR algorithms and
API contracts. Runtime source uses only Julia Base and the bundled Base64
standard library. No external Julia packages, JLL artifacts, QR wrappers,
foreign QR code, downloaded runtime resources, FFI or network services.

Behavioral owner baseline: SpecQR/SpecQR JavaScript
15ad15e5c770ea0e39072f8f88b2733018f02ffd (3.0.0-rc.2), plus reviewed corrections
for high-level FNC1 literal percent, consecutive group separators, Digital Link
dot-value data loss, ambiguous resolver prefixes, finite print diagnostics and
invalid error-correction names. Read-only reviewed Python, Pascal, Elixir and
TypeScript implementations were used as behavioral references.

QR block tables, BCH, placement and Reed-Solomon parameters are normative data.
The 6,953-scalar QR Kanji table reproduces the owner's pinned WHATWG Shift_JIS
first mapping. Mapping data SHA-256:
be0a434df7babc88848f0930ceb3ea9424c6715d89ed4b1b19bcb416f9892fa8
Digital Link implements a documented strict ASCII authority profile.

Reference fixtures, Nayuki QR Code Generator, ZXing-C++, ZXing Java and SVG
rasterizers are development-only verification resources with their own
licenses. None is a runtime dependency. Compiler/decoder binaries are not
included in this source package.
